&Q000510

{1 = 1-10}
9=1.	Shepherd, called by name, for whom holy @wDN{An} has determined in heaven a great destiny! 
13=2.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, called by name, 
17=3.	for whom holy @wDN{An} has determined in heaven a great destiny! 
21=4.	Prince who achieved kingship when still in the true womb, you grandly exercise lordship over the numerous people. 
25=5.	In @wSN{Larsam}, the …… mountain befitting the princely divine powers, 
29=6.	you are truly called to be shepherd of @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 
33=7.	Great @wDN{An}, august in heaven and earth, lord who is wise in everything, 
37=8.	father of the gods, has determined to fix the destinies for that place, 
41=9.	never interrupting the uttering of weighty commands, 
45=10.	…… in the pure interior of heaven. 

{11 = 11-28}
49=11.	Prince @wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, you are the shepherd, the desire of his heart. 
53=12.	May great @wDN{An} manifest brilliantly his heart's love for you; may he bless you for your justice. 
57=13.	May @wDN{An} in his profound heart make the days of your life abundant for you, 
61=14.	and give you kingship over the widespread lands until distant days. 
65=15.	With his holy words may he determine for you a destiny of life, 
69=16.	and with a wholly unalterable command give you long life in addition. 
73=17.	May he fix the holy headdress on your head, 
77=18.	and seat you grandly on the throne of life. 
81=19.	May he hand over to you the sceptre of justice, 
85=20.	and suspend by your side the staff which strengthens the Land. 
89=21.	May he make you grasp the shepherd's crook that causes the people to multiply. 
93=22.	May he open for you the breasts of the brilliant heavens, 
97=23.	and cause the rain to rain for you. 
101=24.	From the heart of heaven may he assemble for you years of abundance and days of plenty. 
105=25.	May he make splendid radiance and heart's joy for your days, 
109=26.	and place in your hands an agreeable reign of justice. 
113=27.	May the great @wDN{An} forever be the protector of your kingship! 
117=28.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, you are my king! 

{29 = 29}
123=29.	28 lines. A prayer to @wDN{An}. 
